<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content="RetailPulse portfolio executive brief: data engineering pipeline, audit reconciliation, and model evaluation" />
    <title>RetailPulse | Portfolio Architecture &amp; Analytical Brief</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        --ink: #10233f;
        --muted: #5a6b82;
        --canvas: #f6f8fb;
        --panel: #ffffff;
        --line: #dfe5ef;
        --blue: #2563eb;
        --blue-tint: #eff4fe;
        --teal: #0f766e;
        --teal-tint: #ecfdf5;
        --amber: #b45309;
        --amber-tint: #fffbeb;
        --rose: #be123c;.8
        --purple: #6366f1;
        --purple-tint: #f5f3ff;
        --shadow: 0 10px 28px rgba(16, 35, 63, 0.06);
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--canvas);
        font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .shell { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 36px 24px 64px; }
      header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-start;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 24px;
        padding-bottom: 24px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }
      .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        color: var(--blue);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.8vw, 3.1rem);
        line-height: 1.05;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }
      .sub {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 12px 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .badge-brief {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
        background: #f1f5f9;
        color: #334155;
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 8px 14px;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      .snapshot-bar {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
        margin: 22px 0 16px;
      }
      .chip {
        background: var(--blue-tint);
        color: #1e40af;
        border: 1px solid #dbeafe;
        border-radius: 999px;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        padding: 6px 12px;
      }

      /* Sections & Cards */
      .section { margin-top: 36px; }
      .section-head { margin-bottom: 16px; }
      .section-head h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      }
      .section-head p {
        margin: 4px 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
      .grid { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
      .metrics-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .card {
        background: var(--panel);
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 16px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        padding: 22px;
      }
      .metric-label {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        font-weight: 750;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }
      .metric-val {
        margin: 8px 0 6px;
        font-size: 1.95rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }
      .metric-note {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.83rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
      }

      /* Static Notice Banner & Provenance Metadata */
      .static-notice-banner {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: 14px;
        background: #fffbeb;
        border: 1px solid #fde68a;
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 14px 18px;
        margin: 16px 0 28px;
        color: #92400e;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .notice-badge {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        background: #d97706;
        color: #ffffff;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        padding: 4px 8px;
        border-radius: 6px;
      }
      .provenance-meta {
        margin-top: 12px;
        padding-top: 8px;
        border-top: 1px dashed var(--line);
        font-size: 0.73rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.45;
      }
      .provenance-meta b {
        color: #334155;
      }
      .provenance-meta code {
        font-family: inherit;
        background: #f1f5f9;
        color: #0f172a;
        padding: 1px 4px;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
      }

      /* Lineage Flow Diagram */
      .lineage-card {
        padding: 24px;
        background: var(--panel);
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 16px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      }
      .flow-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
        gap: 12px;
        margin-top: 14px;
        align-items: stretch;
      }
      .flow-node {
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 12px;
        background: #fafcff;
        padding: 14px;
        position: relative;
      }
      .flow-node b {
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        color: var(--ink);
        margin-bottom: 4px;
      }
      .flow-node span {
        font-size: 0.76rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.35;
        display: block;
      }
      .dbt-banner {
        margin-top: 16px;
        padding: 12px 16px;
        background: var(--amber-tint);
        border: 1px solid #fde68a;
        border-radius: 10px;
        color: #92400e;
        font-size: 0.84rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }

      /* Evidence Cluster Cards */
      .evidence-card {
        border-top: 4px solid var(--blue);
      }
      .evidence-card.model-cluster {
        border-top-color: var(--purple);
      }
      .badge-tag {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 3px 8px;
        border-radius: 6px;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .tag-blue { background: #dbeafe; color: #1e40af; }
      .tag-purple { background: #ede9fe; color: #5b21b6; }
      .audit-list {
        margin: 12px 0 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }
      .audit-list li {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: flex-start;
        padding: 8px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line);
        font-size: 0.86rem;
      }
      .audit-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
      .audit-label { color: var(--muted); }
      .audit-val { font-weight: 700; text-align: right; }

      /* Interactive Budget Selector */
      .btn-group {
        display: inline-flex;
        background: #e2e8f0;
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 4px;
        gap: 4px;
      }
      .btn-pill {
        border: none;
        background: transparent;
        padding: 7px 16px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #475569;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: all 0.15s ease-in-out;
      }
      .btn-pill.active {
        background: var(--blue);
        color: #ffffff;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.3);
      }
      .comparison-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        margin-top: 14px;
        font-size: 0.88rem;
      }
      .comparison-table th {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 9px 12px;
        background: #f8fafc;
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }
      .comparison-table td {
        padding: 11px 12px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }
      .callout {
        border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
        background: var(--amber-tint);
        border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
        padding: 14px 18px;
        color: #78350f;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
        margin-top: 16px;
      }

      /* Charts & Distribution Rows */
      .chart-head {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        margin-bottom: 14px;
      }
      .chart-head b { font-size: 0.98rem; }
      .chart-head span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; }
      .waterfall { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
      .bar-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr 100px;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 12px;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }
      .track { height: 10px; overflow: hidden; background: #edf1f7; border-radius: 99px; }
      .fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 99px; }
      .fill-blue { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #3b82f6, #60a5fa); }
      .fill-rose { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e11d48, #fb7185); }
      .fill-teal { background: linear-gradient(90deg, #0d9488, #2dd4bf); }

      .donut-wrap {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 24px;
        margin-top: 6px;
      }
      .donut {
        flex: 0 0 130px;
        width: 130px; height: 130px; border-radius: 50%;
        background: conic-gradient(var(--teal) 0 25.2%, var(--amber) 25.2% 34.6%, var(--rose) 34.6% 100%);
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        position: relative;
      }
      .donut-hole {
        width: 86px; height: 86px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: #fff;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        text-align: center;
        box-shadow: inset 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
      }
      .donut-hole b {
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        color: var(--ink);
        line-height: 1.1;
      }
      .donut-hole span {
        font-size: 0.68rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.1;
        margin-top: 2px;
      }
      .legend { flex: 1; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
      .legend-item { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; font-size: 0.84rem; }
      .dot { width: 9px; height: 9px; display: inline-block; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 6px; }

      footer {
        margin-top: 48px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.83rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      @media (max-width: 900px) {
        .metrics-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
        .two-col, .flow-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      }
      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .shell { padding: 24px 16px 48px; }
        header { display: block; }
        .badge-brief { display: inline-block; margin-top: 14px; }
        .metrics-4 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .donut-wrap { flex-direction: column; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="shell">
      <header>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">RetailPulse / Portfolio Executive Brief</p>
          <h1>RetailPulse Pipeline &amp; Model Evaluation</h1>
          <p class="sub">
            Data engineering pipeline, audit reconciliation, and historical repurchase backtesting derived from the
            <strong>Online Retail II</strong> dataset (2009–2011). Serves as an executive portfolio brief.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="badge-brief">Portfolio Brief</span>
      </header>

      <div class="snapshot-bar">
        <span class="chip">Source Dataset: Online Retail II</span>
        <span class="chip">Event Span: 2009–2011</span>
        <span class="chip">Engine: PostgreSQL + Python</span>
        <span class="chip">Quality Adapter: dbt core</span>
        <span class="chip">Governed Analytics: Power BI PBIP</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Static Artifact Notice -->
      <div class="static-notice-banner" role="note">
        <span class="notice-badge">Static Snapshot</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Pre-Rendered Analytical Brief:</strong>
          All figures on this page are <em>frozen historical metrics</em> generated from recorded pipeline run <code>{{RUN_ID}}</code> ({{PIPELINE_RUN_DATE}}) and model evaluation artifact ({{EVAL_DATE}}).
          This static HTML file is <strong>not</strong> connected to a live operational feed and does <strong>not</strong> auto-refresh with ongoing pipeline runs or Power BI modifications.
          For live interactive exploration, governed semantic models, and cross-filtering, open the Power BI PBIP project in <code>powerbi/</code>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Executive Numbers -->
      <section class="grid metrics-4" aria-label="Executive numbers">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="metric-label">Gross sales</div>
          <div class="metric-val">$20.81m</div>
          <p class="metric-note">Event-date transaction amount before cancellations.</p>
          <div class="provenance-meta">
            <b>Source:</b> <code>mart.revenue_daily</code> / <code>bi.sales_daily</code><br />
            <b>Grain:</b> Snapshot 1 &times; 604 published days (2009–2011)<br />
            <b>Contract:</b> <code>docs/architecture/MART_REVENUE_DAILY.md</code>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="metric-label">Net transactions</div>
          <div class="metric-val">$19.29m</div>
          <p class="metric-note">Gross sales combined with signed cancellation values.</p>
          <div class="provenance-meta">
            <b>Source:</b> <code>mart.revenue_daily.net_transaction_amount</code><br />
            <b>Calculation:</b> $20.81m gross &minus; $1.53m signed cancellations<br />
            <b>Contract:</b> <code>docs/architecture/KPI_DICTIONARY.md:28</code>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="metric-label">Customer purchase events</div>
          <div class="metric-val">36,969</div>
          <p class="metric-note">Identified customer &times; invoice events after cleaning.</p>
          <div class="provenance-meta">
            <b>Source:</b> <code>int.customer_purchase_event_snapshot</code><br />
            <b>Grain:</b> <code>(customer_id, invoice_no)</code> &bull; Snapshot 1<br />
            <b>Contract:</b> <code>docs/architecture/CUSTOMER_PURCHASE_EVENT.md</code>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="metric-label">RFM customers</div>
          <div class="metric-val">5,878</div>
          <p class="metric-note">Unique eligible customers tracked in snapshot marts.</p>
          <div class="provenance-meta">
            <b>Source:</b> <code>mart.customer_rfm_snapshot</code> / <code>bi.customer_lifecycle_snapshot</code><br />
            <b>Grain:</b> Unique <code>customer_id</code> in Snapshot 1<br />
            <b>Contract:</b> <code>docs/architecture/CUSTOMER_RFM_SNAPSHOT.md</code>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 1: Lineage & System Architecture -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>1. Data Lineage &amp; Pipeline Architecture</h2>
          <p>PostgreSQL migrations and views own transformation logic. dbt acts as a contract test suite and documentation adapter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lineage-card">
          <div class="flow-grid">
            <div class="flow-node">
              <b>1. Excel Snapshot</b>
              <span>Source workbook (.xlsx) validated against source manifest SHA-256.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <b>2. Python Ingestion</b>
              <span>Streaming batch loader (`ops.source_file`) with duplicate protection.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <b>3. PostgreSQL Raw</b>
              <span>Immutable `raw.online_retail_ii` preserves every row and sheet location.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <b>4. Stg / Int / Mart / DW</b>
              <span>PostgreSQL views &amp; materialized relations (`stg`, `int`, `mart`, `dw`).</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <b>5. Decision &amp; BI Views</b>
              <span>Curated `bi.*` semantic views feeding Power BI PBIP and model evaluation.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dbt-banner">
            <strong>Architecture Boundary:</strong> PostgreSQL migrations and views own all transactional transformations.
            <code>dbt</code> operates alongside PostgreSQL as an adapter to verify data contracts (schema tests, uniqueness, accepted values) and expose lineage, not as the transformation engine.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Two Distinct Evidence Clusters -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>2. Audit Evidence &amp; Provenance</h2>
          <p>Two distinct evidence clusters from recorded run logs and model evaluation artifacts. Kept separate by date and operational scope.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid two-col">
          <!-- Cluster 1: Pipeline Orchestration Run -->
          <article class="card evidence-card">
            <span class="badge-tag tag-blue">Pipeline Orchestration Run</span>
            <h3 style="margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 1.15rem;">Run Record: {{PIPELINE_RUN_DATE}}</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.84rem;">Recorded in <code>last_run.json</code> (Run ID: <code>{{RUN_ID}}</code>).</p>
            <ul class="audit-list">
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Execution Status</span>
                <span class="audit-val" style="color: var(--teal);">{{PIPELINE_STATUS}}</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Source vs Raw Rows</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{PIPELINE_ROWS}} (exact match)</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">SQL Quality Gates</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{PIPELINE_SQL_GATES}}</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">dbt Build Status</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{PIPELINE_DBT_STATUS}}</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Execution Time</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{PIPELINE_DURATION}} (end-to-end orchestration)</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p style="margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);">
              <em>Scope:</em> Evidence verifies this specific pipeline execution on {{PIPELINE_RUN_DATE}}; it does not claim unconditional idempotency for future snapshot versions.
            </p>
          </article>

          <!-- Cluster 2: Model Evaluation Artifact -->
          <article class="card evidence-card model-cluster">
            <span class="badge-tag tag-purple">Model Evaluation Artifact</span>
            <h3 style="margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 1.15rem;">Evaluation Artifact: {{EVAL_DATE}}</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.84rem;">Generated at {{EVAL_TIMESTAMP}} via <code>train_repurchase_model.py</code>.</p>
            <ul class="audit-list">
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Target Snapshot</span>
                <span class="audit-val">Snapshot {{SNAPSHOT_ID}} (SHA-256: <code>{{SNAPSHOT_SHA_SHORT}}</code>)</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Hash Manifest Reconciled</span>
                <span class="audit-val" style="color: var(--teal);">Verified match with source manifest</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Temporal Holdout Period</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{HOLDOUT_PERIOD}}</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Holdout Cohort Size</span>
                <span class="audit-val">{{HOLDOUT_COHORT_SIZE}}</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                <span class="audit-label">Observation / Prediction Window</span>
                <span class="audit-val">180 days obs. &rarr; 90 days pred.</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p style="margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--muted);">
              <em>Scope:</em> Historical temporal backtest evaluating repurchase labels in the holdout window. Generated after pipeline run <code>{{RUN_ID}}</code>. Not an operational forecast for active customers.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Revenue & Cancellation Evidence -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2>3. Revenue &amp; Cancellation Evidence</h2>
          <p>Event-date revenue composition and heuristic cancellation diagnostic matching.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid two-col">
          <article class="card">
            <div class="chart-head"><b>Transaction Composition</b><span>USD, rounded</span></div>
            <div class="waterfall">
              <div class="bar-row">
                <span>Gross sales</span>
                <div class="track"><div class="fill fill-blue" style="width: 100%;"></div></div>
                <span style="text-align: right; font-weight: 700;">$20.81m</span>
              </div>
              <div class="bar-row">
                <span>Cancellations</span>
                <div class="track"><div class="fill fill-rose" style="width: 7.3%;"></div></div>
                <span style="text-align: right; font-weight: 700;">&minus;$1.53m</span>
              </div>
              <div class="bar-row">
                <span>Net amount</span>
                <div class="track"><div class="fill fill-teal" style="width: 92.7%;"></div></div>
                <span style="text-align: right; font-weight: 700;">$19.29m</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.83rem;">
              Coverage: 824,364 rows carry Customer ID (77.2%); 243,007 guest rows remain in revenue rather than being discarded.
            </p>
            <div class="provenance-meta">
              <b>Source:</b> <code>stg.online_retail_transaction</code> (1,067,371 rows)<br />
              <b>Contract:</b> Missing customer IDs retained in revenue marts; excluded from customer marts (<code>docs/architecture/STAGING_TRANSACTION_MODEL.md</code>).
            </div>
          </article>
          <!-- Right Card: Cancellation Evidence -->
          <article class="card">
            <div class="chart-head"><b>Cancellation Evidence</b><span>Diagnostic candidate matching</span></div>
            <div class="donut-wrap">
              <div class="donut" role="img" aria-label="25.2 percent matched candidate, 9.4 percent ambiguous, 65.4 percent unmatched">
                <div class="donut-hole">
                  <b>19,494</b>
                  <span>cancellations</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="legend">
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-name"><i class="dot" style="background: var(--teal);"></i>Matched candidate</span><b>4,907</b></div>
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-name"><i class="dot" style="background: var(--amber);"></i>Ambiguous</span><b>1,833</b></div>
                <div class="legend-item"><span class="legend-name"><i class="dot" style="background: var(--rose);"></i>Unmatched</span><b>12,754</b></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin: 14px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.81rem; line-height: 1.45;">
              <em>Diagnostic only:</em> Candidate matching uses snapshot, customer, stock code, and quantity magnitude. It does not prove accounting returns or adjust revenue.
            </p>
            <div class="provenance-meta">
              <b>Source:</b> <code>bi.cancellation_diagnostic</code> &bull; <code>int.cancellation_match_resolution</code> (19,494 cancellation rows)<br />
              <b>Contract:</b> Heuristic candidate edge resolution (<code>docs/architecture/CANCELLATION_MATCH_CANDIDATES.md</code>).
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

